  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the following circuit the switch <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math>is closed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. The charge on the capacitor <math><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> as a function of time will be given by <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\qt0122_646af8476bac.png\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 141px;\" /></p>"
  },
